# `STYLE-KEY-SCOPE`: `style=` LEAVES `field`, `cell` and `signal`. On a field
# it was a correctness defect, not a tidy-up: `field "B" 8 present=""
# style=solid` erased the dash that is conditional presence's only visual
# carrier while the MODEL still recorded the field as conditionally present,
# so one line produced two different figures — `PRESENTATION-AS-MEANING-CARRIER`'s exact prohibition.
# (The flag was spelled `optional` until 0.1, `PRESENCE-CONDITION-EXPRESSION`.) The other two move with it as
# one minimum set (11 in-repo uses, 0 downstream). `style=` stays live on
# node/group/edge/class/bundle/threshold/band; only these three lost it.
# Multi-section (`MULTI-FIGURE-DOCUMENTS`): one file, three genres, three diagnostics.
figdown 0.1 bitfield
bitfield b "B" word=8 numbering=msb0
field "A" 8 present="" style=solid
field "B" 8
figdown 0.1 table
table t "T"
| a | b |
|---|---|
| 1 | 2 |
cell (1,1) style=dashed
figdown 0.1 timing
timing w "W"
signal clk pppp style=dotted
signal en  01..
